## What belongs here

A surprise, not a rule. "The staging DB has no `uuid-ossp`, so generate UUIDs in app code" is a gotcha. "Always generate UUIDs in app code" is a decision — that goes in `decisions.md`.

One line for the trap, one for what to do instead. If the explanation is long, link `docs/dev/`.

When a gotcha stops being true — the dependency was fixed, the environment changed — delete it. A stale trap is worse than none, because it is believed.

